# Expected digests for the files behind rows in dataset_candidates.csv.
#
# Standard sha256sum format, so this file is BOTH machine-read by
# calibration/scripts/vcholerae_pilot.py and directly usable by hand:
#
#     cd ~/biofilm-pilot-data
#     sha256sum -c /path/to/dataset_candidates.sha256 --ignore-missing
#
# The digests previously existed only inside the free-text `rationale` column
# of dataset_candidates.csv. Parsing a digest out of prose is not verification,
# and a chain of custody that stops at "the ledger says so" has a gap exactly
# where it matters. The chain is now:
#
#     Dryad identity -> retrieved bytes -> verified SHA-256 -> reader metadata
#     -> declared segmentation basis -> derived output
#
# vcholerae_dryad_zcrjdfnph — Dryad doi:10.5061/dryad.zcrjdfnph, CC0-1.0.
# Retrieved by browser 2026-08-15 (the download route is fronted by an Anubis
# proof-of-work challenge aimed at automated clients, which was deliberately
# not defeated). All four verified against the ledger on that date.
276a689d37b28a144bd75b785981e355528f174b45b4700fe105d702947b9537  Dataset_1_Fig1b_Timecourse.nd2
0f19ca0b2e04b583ba61dc668a62abcd300ec5e01ecc897245a0057701327748  Dataset_2_Fig4a_Timecourse.nd2
